  "methodology": "Other",
  "methodology_other": "Data were collected from the UNDP 2005 Population Report, the Population Estimation Survey of Somalia from the Somalia Directorate of National Statistics, the Early Warning Disease Surveillance and  Response Bulletin, the First Malaria Indicator Survey in Somalia, the Armed Conflict Location and Event Data Project, Mobility of the Somali People from the Somalia Directorate of National Statistics, the People in Need Data: Humanitarian Needs Overview Somalia from the United Nations Office for the Coordination of Humanitarian Affairs, the Integrated Food Security Phase Classification, and the Somalia Joint Multi Cluster Needs Assessment. Census Bureau staff altered boundaries and modified the statistical data as detailed in the Metadata tab of the tabular data.",
  "name": "somalia-subnational-boundaries-and-tabular-data",
  "notes": "The geodatabase contains boundaries for the national and first- and second-order administrative divisions, aligned to the Large Scale International Boundaries dataset from the U.S. Department of State. The feature classes are suitable for linking to the attribute data provided.\r\n\r\nThe tabular data contain total population for 2005 (population estimates) and 2014 (population estimates), as well as information relating to education, health, malaria, conflict, insecurity, stresses, and needs. ",
